From 06ef896c62597d200aad1d95f3063f0611fbac2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:09:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/46] glm5-next: KDA prologue in the gated delta net op,
 split-K hc_fn matvec

KDA (n_seq_tokens <= 8, state read through ids): ggml_gated_delta_net_set_kda_prologue
moves the q/k l2 norms, the decay gate lb*sigmoid(-(g + dt_b)*A) and the beta
sigmoid into the GDN op (src[7] = A, src[8] = dt_b), same f32 operations as the
graph; the CPU reference is bit-identical to the unfused chain. -6 dispatches per
KDA layer at n=3 (RMS_NORM_SCALE x2, ADD, MUL, SCALE_SIGMOID_SCALE, SIGMOID).
LLAMA_KDA_PROLOGUE=0 restores the separate ops.

mHC hc_fn (24 rows, k 16384): for <= 8 tokens the q8_0 matvec runs as
GGML_OP_DSV4_HC_MIX_PARTIALS, one workgroup per 512-element K slice (and 8
tokens), writing per-slice partial dot products plus the slice's sum of squares;
DSV4_HC_PRE_MIX sums the slices and takes r from the summed squares, so there is
no extra reduce dispatch. LLAMA_HC_MIX_SPLIT=0 keeps the plain matvec.

halo port: the test struct keeps q27-tune's kda flag next to the new prologue flag; the unused A / dt_b
bindings take the read-only state buffer as their dummy, as q27-tune does for ids.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
